 "audience": "general",
 "facts": "Emu War, Campion district, Western Australia, 2 Nov - 10 Dec 1932. About 20,000 emus; farmers were WWI veterans; emus ate wheat and broke fences (letting rabbits in). Defence Minister Sir George Pearce sent Major G.P.W. Meredith with two soldiers, two Lewis guns, 10,000 rounds. 2 Nov: ~50 emus split into small groups. 4 Nov: ambush at a dam, 1,000+ emus, gun jammed. Gun mounted on a truck: could not catch the birds, ride too rough to aim. Withdrawn 8 Nov after ~2,500 rounds. Second attempt to 10 Dec: Meredith reported 986 birds for 9,860 rounds. He compared their toughness to tanks. Minimal effect on emu numbers. (Wikipedia 'Emu War', Britannica, Australian Geographic)",
 "outro_text": "Dig deeper with Sir Digsworth!",
